                <pb facs="0427" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.796/21: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-28T20:00:00-04:00">October 28, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. Your 361, October 24, 9 p.m. The War Department has not agreed to the
                    proposed use of Roberts Field by BOAC land planes and is taking up the matter
                    with representatives of British Air Ministry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
